scenario w2-bare-window-target
# W2: a bare `-t @W` resolves to the most recently active session holding W.
# After the laptop types in its grouped session, the device's tab switch moves
# the laptop's window instead of the device's own. `$S:@W` targets the issuer.
session O 80x24 w0
window O w1
group U O
tty laptop U 200x50
control device O
send device select-window -t {w1}
expect-current O w1
send device select-window -t {w0}
expect-current O w0
key laptop
send device select-window -t {w1}
expect device %session-window-changed {U} {w1}
expect-current U w1
expect-current O w0
expect-latest w1 device
send device select-window -t '{O}:{w1}'
expect device %session-window-changed {O} {w1}
expect-current O w1
